========================================================================================================================
1.  THE ADMISSION RULE, AND WHAT IT DOES TO ITEM 100's LADDER
========================================================================================================================
  An a_0 measurement is admitted as M/L-FREE here if its MEASURED leverage |d log a_0/d log Upsilon| <= 0.20,
  i.e. a factor-2 error in the stellar mass-to-light ratio moves it by less than 0.06 dex.  The leverage is
  not asserted for any rung: item 102 measured it for the deep tail by re-running at fixed sample, item 111
  measured it for every KiDS bin by rescaling the adopted baryonic mass, item 105 measured it for the BTFR.
  
    R1's leverage measured at fixed sample by re-running at Upsilon = 0.4/0.5/0.6: d log a_0/d log Upsilon = -0.146  (item 102 got -0.148)
  
    measurement                                                  a_0   +-dex  |lever|   M/L-free?  provenance
    SPARC deep tail, f_*,loc < 0.2                         7.361e-11   0.065    0.146       ADMIT  h102 (re-derived above)
    SPARC gas-dominated discs, outermost point             7.816e-11   0.080    0.182       ADMIT  h124 rung A (re-derived)
    SPARC BTFR, f_gas>0.7, C removed                       7.156e-11   0.080    0.180       ADMIT  h105 part E (re-derived)
    KiDS-1000 lensing, shape-only a_0                      6.310e-11   0.300    0.000       ADMIT  h113 check 113-D2
    ALFALFA gas-dominated (f_* < 0.15), all baryons        5.820e-11   0.250    0.110       ADMIT  h124 rung B table
    Leisman almost-darks, ceiling-matched                  3.110e-11   0.130    0.000       ADMIT  h124 rung C / item 31b
    Lelli tidal dwarfs, external field included            1.734e-11   0.170    0.000       ADMIT  h124 rung D
    KiDS-1000 dwarf lens stack                             9.550e-11   0.109    1.046      reject  h1_h66_h2_h65 item 2; lever from h111-A
    SPARC full deep tail, full kernel                      9.040e-11   0.038    0.647      reject  h102 sec.2; lever h121a
    SPARC full deep tail, item 25 as published             1.146e-10   0.043    0.647      reject  item 25; +0.10 dex estimator bias, h102 sec.0
    SPARC BTFR all 122, C removed                          9.818e-11   0.029    0.591      reject  h105 check 105-C
    KiDS colour bins (blue / red)                          8.840e-11   0.052    1.046      reject  h111 fig-8; red bin 2.83e-10
    KiDS Sersic bins (disc / bulge)                        1.060e-10   0.048    1.046      reject  h112 fig-8; bulge bin 2.53e-10
    SPARC closed-form inversion at R_eff                   1.176e-10   0.056    0.647      reject  h101; f_DM carries a stellar mass model
    RC100 closed-form inversion at R_e                     1.385e-10   0.070    0.647      reject  h101; same
    Li+2020 halo product 2 pi G rho_0 r_0                  1.690e-10   1.200    0.647      reject  h106; profile-choice systematic 1.2 dex
  [PASS] 1.1 ITEM 100's HEADLINE IS WITHDRAWN, and it is my own workflow's number.  Item 100 wrote that 'the two measurements that do NOT lean on a stellar M/L -- the gas-dominated deep tail and the dwarf lens stack -- agree to 0.08 dex'.  NEITHER of those two is M/L-free on a measured leverage: the deep tail as item 25 ran it carries -0.647 (h121a) and the KiDS dwarf lens stack carries -1.046 (h111-A, where a deep-MOND lensing a_0 is degenerate with the assumed baryonic mass at exponent 1).  The sentence that organised two ledgers is false   (deep tail lever -0.647, dwarf lens stack lever -1.046, both above the 0.20 admission threshold; and their 0.08 dex agreement is itself an artefact -- the deep-tail value in it (1.14e-10) carried the +0.10 dex estimator bias h102 found)
  [PASS] 1.2 the admission rule keeps something: 7 of the 16 measurements in the hunt clear |lever| <= 0.20, so the M/L-free ladder is not empty -- but 3 of the 7 are the SAME 20-23 SPARC gas-rich discs seen through different estimators, which is a fact section 3 has to handle rather than average over   (7 admitted of 16; admitted rungs R1,R2,R3 share SPARC galaxies)

========================================================================================================================
2.  ITEM 123 -- THE TWO FOOTINGS, DECIDED?
========================================================================================================================
  canonical a_0 = 9.360e-11 (log -10.0287) | alt a_0 = 1.130e-10 (log -9.9469)
  they are 0.0818 dex apart, so a 3 sigma decision needs a TOTAL error of 0.0273 dex = 6.5% on an M/L-free measurement of a_0

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2A.  the coherent floor, built here from sensitivities this script measures (item 103 is not used)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    the kernel's mean local log-slope on the R1 points: <n> = <d log nu/d log y> = -0.4525 (the deep-MOND limit is -1/2)
    analytic, from d/d log a of the estimating equation:  d log a_0/d log D      = 1/<n> = -2.210
                                                          d log a_0/d log M_gas  = (1+<n>)/<n> x (gas share)
    numerical, scaling every distance by 1.05: d log a_0/d log D = -2.246  (item 103 measured -2.254 independently)
  [PASS] 2A.1 the distance sensitivity is the analytic 1/<n>, not the textbook deep-MOND -2 -- so the deep tail's a_0 inherits 2.2x the distance ladder's fractional error, not 2x.  Derived and measured two ways here, so it does not depend on item 103, whose win did not survive verification   (numerical -2.246 vs analytic 1/<n> = -2.210)
    numerical, scaling the HI mass scale by 1.1: d log a_0/d log M_gas = -1.107 (gas supplies 85% of g_bar on these points)
  [PASS] 2A.2 THE PRICE OF REMOVING THE STELLAR M/L, and it is the sharpest new number in item 123.  Cutting to points where stars supply under 20% of g_bar drops the Upsilon leverage to 0.15 -- but it RAISES the HI mass scale's leverage to very nearly 1.2, because the same gas now supplies almost all of g_bar.  The measurement does not become calibration-free; it trades a stellar calibration for a hydrogen one, at higher leverage   (d log a_0/d log M_gas = -1.107 against d log a_0/d log Upsilon = -0.146; gas is 85% of g_bar)
    inclination: V_obs ~ 1/sin i so g_obs ~ sin^-2 i and d log a_0/d log sin i = 2/<n> = -4.420 (median inclination of the R1 sample 60 deg)
      optimistic  (distance scale 2%, HI mass scale 0.03 dex, inclination zero-point 1 deg) -> distance 0.0193, gas 0.0332, inclination 0.0190  TOTAL 0.0428 dex
      realistic   (distance scale 5%, HI mass scale 0.05 dex, inclination zero-point 2 deg) -> distance 0.0476, gas 0.0554, inclination 0.0371  TOTAL 0.0819 dex
  [PASS] 2A.3 the COHERENT floor under any M/L-free deep-tail a_0 is dominated by the HI mass scale, not by anything stellar and not by the distance scale.  Even on the optimistic budget it exceeds the 0.027 dex a 3 sigma footing decision needs, so NO amount of extra galaxies can decide the footings by this route   (optimistic floor 0.0428 dex, realistic 0.0819 dex, against the 0.0273 dex a 3 sigma decision requires)

