  [PASS] 2B.1 ITEM 123's OWN CRITERION, and it is NOT met.  On the headline M/L-free measurement -- the SPARC deep tail with the stellar share of g_bar under 20% -- NEITHER footing is excluded at 3 sigma once the coherent calibration floor is carried.  The measured value sits BELOW both, by 1.0 sigma and 1.8 sigma respectively, so the most that can be said is that it leans canonical.  Note which two rungs DO exclude both footings at over 3 sigma: the almost-darks and the tidal dwarfs, the two item 124 identified as non-measurements   (a_0 = 7.361e-11 +- 0.1044 dex total: canonical -1.00 sigma, alt -1.78 sigma)

